Lexington County","/arc-plc/south-carolina/lexington-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record from 1951 to 2025 shows October to November came in under 90% of normal in 42 of 75 years on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 10 grids. In 2025, the middle of the grids got 65% of normal in October to November and 47% in November to December. So far in 2026, March to April came in at 25% of normal on the middle of the grids. Every grid in the county had its driest year in 1954.</p>"}
